      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While waiting a day or two might not harm, it's still essential to see a doctor to determine the cause of your symptoms and rule out any underlying conditions. Even if it's a nerve issue, some cases of Bell's palsy can be accompanied by underlying conditions that need attention. Going to the ER isn't \"dramatic,\" and a visit can provide reassurance and guidance. A doctor can also discuss treatment options, such as medications or physical therapy, depending on the underlying cause of your symptoms.",
