      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's understandable to want to manage the issue at home, taking vitamins or ibuprofen will not address the underlying cause of your symptoms. Bell's palsy is an autoimmune condition that may have an underlying trigger or predisposing factor, and using over-the-counter medications won't diagnose or treat the condition. Taking those unless strictly necessary can actually mask potential underlying issues, and going to the ER might be a safer bet to determine the cause.",
